course: dictionary
lesson: 2000
title: Finding the right meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Children who skip breakfast find it harder to concentrate and can feel faint by mid-morning.» Here concentrate means to give all your attention to one thing. Try your meaning in the sentence: "find it harder to pay attention" still makes sense, so you have the right one.
explain: The same word can work in other ways. In a science lesson, a concentrated solution has a lot of dissolved substance in little water. When you see concentrate, ask yourself: is someone talking about attention, a strong liquid, or something being gathered together?
fact: Concentrate (verb) means to give all your attention and thinking to one thing.
fact: Concentrate can also mean to bring or gather many things or people into one place, or to make a liquid stronger by removing water.
fact: Concentrate (noun) means a strong form of a liquid that you add water to before using, like juice concentrate.
fact: Sleep, food, water and exercise help you concentrate.
fact: «Too little sleep makes it harder to concentrate»; children of 9 or 10 need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep a night.
exercise: «I can't concentrate with this noise.» What does concentrate mean here? | Gather people into one place | Sing very loudly | *Give all your attention to one thing | Make a drink stronger by taking out water
exercise: Mum says, «Add water to the orange concentrate.» What is the concentrate? | A type of fruit | A tin of paint | A small paper cup | *A strong liquid that you add water to
exercise: Which of these helps you concentrate? | Playing loud music while you work | Staying up very late every night | Skipping breakfast and lunch | *Good sleep, food and water
test: In a science lesson, a «concentrated solution» has a lot of what? | Water and no substance at all | *Dissolved substance in very little water | Air bubbles | Ice
test: Which is the safe habit when crossing the road? | Running across as fast as you can | Looking at your phone | Closing your eyes | *Concentrating, with no phone in your hand
exam: Which word means to give all your attention to one thing? | Dilute | Burnout | *Concentrate | Scatter
